  - Damm check digit
abstract: >-
  A national address model and registry for Togo: every compound in the country (2,768,053 at issue) has a code made
  of a place name people already say and a number of four or five digits read in pairs, unique in the whole country on
  its own. Where the State gives an address (Lomé's streets, the District Autonome du Grand Lomé's entrance addresses
  once released), it is shown first. The repository holds the full registry, the reference engine, a ready-made
  registry server and API, and the paper in English and French.
